<urn:beads-cache:finding:C4-FTQ-001> triage:qa6Review "{\"owner\": \"background C2 rust-developer, with upstream public compatibility restoration owned by sc-runtime\", \"qa_pass\": \"qa-6\", \"reviewed_commit\": \"08f7cee0308f52eb0a5a0067cb4e209e2c82806e\", \"reviewer_records\": [{\"finding\": {\"category\": \"tests\", \"evidence\": \"Current start uses run_with_cleanup_and_bound; scenario receives the actual runtime endpoint and attempts a competing TcpListener::bind(address), requiring AddrInUse. Released builder.rs retains listener ownership during on_bound and through serve. No reservation/drop/rebind, bind retry or widened timer remains. Current Linux/macOS E0425 at106 prevents execution; source correction is credited without claiming a passing lifecycle sample.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-daemon/src/readiness_tests/runtime_lifecycle.rs\", \"id\": \"C4-FTQ-001\", \"issue\": \"The old free/rebind endpoint race is removed in source, but the required new continuously-owned-listener positive/competing-bind negative has not executed for the current candidate because the same lifecycle test fails compilation at its public timeout-helper call.\", \"line\": 66, \"recommendation\": \"Preserve port0, runtime-owned endpoint notification, deterministic AddrInUse negative, actual production signals/cleanup/instance lock and same-endpoint restart; qualify the unchanged controls after consuming the approved public helper restoration.\", \"severity\": \"important\"}, \"reviewer\": \"rust-qa-agent\"}, {\"finding\": {\"evidence\": \"consumer_checks.py360-364 closes the sole socket before configuring its captured port; first daemon spawn is423 and probe425 only addresses the released port. Independent bounded negative used the actual ab7 candidate daemon (sha2569f31735d7c140bf45c5b939a35b284658ae26d410104879ad5c3ad89304dd29b): reserve port0, close reservation, keep self-owned competitor bound, launch daemon once. It returned1 with RUNTIME.BIND_FAILED/AddrInUse, empty stdout, in0.195867958s; child reaped and scratch removed. Raw proof: flaky-port-handoff-probe.json/.log. Initial sandbox bind denial is separately preserved; one identical authorized native-context execution followed. This proves the fixture interleaving, not a product defect or full acceptance execution.\", \"file\": \"scripts/consumer_checks.py\", \"id\": \"C4-FTQ-001\", \"issue\": \"A remaining in-scope occurrence releases its ephemeral port reservation before any daemon spawn. Another listener can acquire that address during the intervening config/CLI/cache work. The real daemon then correctly exits with bind failure while acceptance waits for health; a compatible unrelated listener could also satisfy the unowned health probe. The original runtime_lifecycle occurrence is source-corrected, but that does not correct this required process acceptance occurrence.\", \"line\": 360, \"mechanism\": \"parallel_race\", \"recommendation\": \"Remove the reserve/free assumption from process acceptance. Use an approved public runtime-owned endpoint notification/ownership path with a bounded serving handshake tied to the actual child, or split/rewrite the scenario so a collision-safe explicit endpoint check is not represented as reserved endpoint ownership. Route any missing process-facing capability to its owner. Preserve real daemon signals, cleanup, instance-lock and restart assertions; no port retries, random-port loops, sleeps or wider budgets.\", \"severity\": \"important\", \"source_correction_credit\": \"runtime_lifecycle.rs66-88 now receives the actual continuously owned endpoint through run_with_cleanup_and_bound;209-216 tests competing bind. owned_runtime.rs35-75 likewise uses public start_with_cleanup and a competing bind. Those source corrections are real; affected execution is blocked by the absent published instrument_router.\", \"status\": \"open_remaining_process_fixture_occurrence\", \"test\": \"installed daemon process acceptance\"}, \"reviewer\": \"flaky-test-qa\"}], \"scope\": \"Preserve occurrence-specific source corrections and actual platform limits; final sole-enforcer report pending publication.\", \"screen\": \"all_not_applicable; no waiver or suppression\", \"severity\": \"Important\", \"status\": \"open\"}" .

